  "title": "Can banks fund the next investment cycle?",
  "summary": "The widening gap between credit and deposit growth does not, by itself, mean that banks are running out of funds or are unable to lend. The overall credit-deposit ratio remains a measure of the relationship between outstanding loans and deposits, not a direct measure of lending capacity. Nevertheless, the divergence makes deposit mobilisation and the management of incremental funding increasingly important.",
